### Internationalization

```typescript
// ✅ Use @wordpress/i18n for all user-facing strings
import { __ } from '@wordpress/i18n';

const message = __('Debug log cleared successfully', 'debug-suite');
const contextual = _x('Settings', 'menu item', 'debug-suite');
```

## Directory Structure Standards

```md
includes/
├── Services/                    # Business logic services
│   ├── ServiceInterface.php    # Service marker interface
│   ├── ExampleService.php      # Individual services
│   └── DebugLog/               # Feature-specific services
├── API/                        # REST controllers only
│   ├── RestController.php      # Base controller
│   └── ExampleController.php   # Individual controllers
├── Providers/                  # Service providers
│   └── AppServiceProvider.php  # Service registration
└── Core/
    ├── ServiceResponse.php     # Response wrapper
    └── Container/              # DI container system

src/
├── pages/[feature-name]/       # Feature pages
│   ├── index.tsx              # Main component
│   ├── types.ts               # TypeScript types
│   ├── hooks.ts               # Custom hooks
│   └── components/            # Feature components
│       ├── feature-viewer.tsx # Display component
│       └── feature-controls.tsx # Controls component
└── components/ui/             # Reusable UI components
```

## Helper Functions Usage

### PHP Helpers

```php
// ✅ Use debug suite helpers
$service = debug_suite_resolve(ExampleService::class);
$container = debug_suite_container();

// ✅ DI definition helpers
$definition = debug_suite_autowire_with_params(LoggerService::class, [
    'log_level' => 'debug'
], true); // singleton

// ✅ Environment-aware configuration
$config = debug_suite_autowire_env(DatabaseService::class, [
    'development' => ['debug' => true],
    'production' => ['debug' => false]
]);
```

## Error Handling Patterns

### Service Layer Error Handling

```php
// ✅ Always return ServiceResponse, never throw exceptions to controllers
if (!file_exists($file_path)) {
    return ServiceResponse::failure(
        __('File not found.', 'debug-suite'),
        'file_not_found',
        ['path' => $file_path] // Context data
    );
}

// ✅ Success responses with data
return ServiceResponse::success([
    'data' => $processed_data,
    'timestamp' => current_time('mysql')
]);
```

### Frontend Error Handling

```typescript
// ✅ Handle API errors gracefully
try {
    const response = await apiClient.getData();
    if (response.success) {
        setData(response.data);
    } else {
        setError(response.message);
    }
} catch (error) {
    setError(__('An unexpected error occurred', 'debug-suite'));
}
```

## Testing Standards

### PHP Unit Tests

```php
/**
 * @covers \DebugSuite\Services\ExampleService
 * @group services
 * @group unit
 */
class ExampleServiceTest extends DebugSuiteTestCase {
    
    public function test_process_data_success(): void {
        $service = new ExampleService();
        $result = $service->process_data(['required_field' => 'value']);
        
        $this->assertTrue($result->is_success());
        $this->assertArrayHasKey('data', $result->to_array());
    }
}
```

## Performance & Security

### Security Practices

```php
// ✅ Always sanitize and validate input
$safe_path = $this->sanitize_path($relative_path);
if (!$this->is_path_safe($full_path)) {
    return ServiceResponse::failure('Invalid path', 'invalid_path');
}

// ✅ Check permissions
if (!current_user_can('manage_options')) {
    return new WP_Error('permission_denied', 'Insufficient permissions');
}
```

### Performance Optimization

```php
// ✅ Use container singleton pattern
$container->singleton(ExpensiveService::class, fn() => new ExpensiveService());

// ✅ Cache reflection for autowiring
private array $reflection_cache = [];
```

